[Applause]  MLB the show has always been interested  in creating a hard-hitting realistic and  most of all an immersive baseball game  the PlayStation exclusive comes in hot  next month with its latest entry in the  series MLB the show 19 and there are a  lot of improvements you can look forward  to one of the biggest changes has to be  the overhauled system that the show 19  uses for its defensive players  everyone loves seamed studs out there in  the outfield flashing the leather and  making spectacular catches replicating  these moments in game feels great but  you can't have every player have the  same skill tier as say a Matt Chapman  that's why the devs behind the show make  sure that skill differences on defense  and your ability matters so much more  all the attributes that contribute to  your defensive player success are closer  to their real-life counterparts so if  you have your stud left fielder suddenly  playing on the opposite side of the  field odds are you may be prone to  mistakes players with lower skill  attributes may even get a bad jump  towards the ball and with over 1300 new  animations your fielders can put in some  serious work to help you make a double  play that'll get your blood pumping with  all the defensive improvements in play  let's talk about something else in  baseball that everyone loves contact  that bat the show 19 is introduced the  method that rewards your skill at  batting and lets you improve by judging  how you swing and even how well you can  take your pitches after all even the  pros are making only about 30% of their  hits so how do you balance this in a way  to where you can feel empowered and can  start making meaningful hits well you  make contact hitters matter baseball  players who are known to spread the ball  out with SiC line drives are on  different pockmarks of the field are now  more relevant than ever before by adding  a level of depth to your lineup this  encourages you to play to your bat or  strengths rather than just constantly  mashing or flicking your stick for the  standard swing there's a lot more coming  up with MLB the show 19 the fans of the  series will love to see and we'll have a  lot more to share with you in the near  future stay tuned to games.com for all  the reviews videos and features you love  see you on the Mount  [Applause]  [Music]

